[#:seon.task{:name "acquired-functions-get-no-supplied-defaults"
             :kind :function
             :intent "Call preparation supplies nothing inside any function acquired from program entities: SCI reads the hook from the context the fn closure captured, and acquired functions were analysed in the memoized program base, which holds no custody, so hook passes arguments through. From a REPL deftest (plan-now) calling (my.plan/current) refuses argument count, and ((fn [] (my.plan/current {:seon.agent/id 'root'}))) refuses [:seon.db/db]. It covers another agent calling mine and every call after a reload. Owner decision: hook reads the arming evaluation's environment (~10 lines), S12's wrapper-applied defaults (recommended, ruled plan step), or acquire into each execution's own fork (loses 389 ms -> 29 ms per member)."
             :must-read #{seon.call-preparation/hook seon.call-preparation/supply seon.sci.eval/acquire!}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/landing/agent-test-worlds-2026-09-26.md"
                         "docs/seon/issues/an-agents-test-world-has-no-agent-so-my-functions-cannot-be-tested-as-documented.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "supply-reads-the-connection-head"
             :kind :function
             :intent "The hook plans and supplies against the connection's head, not the evaluation's working value, so a my.* read inside a run (tests-reaching after a defn in the same run) misses entities the run already wrote (D7). a44538acc fixed the older-value half only."
             :must-read #{seon.call-preparation/hook seon.call-preparation/snapshot}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/landing/fix-dogfood-api-2026-09-26.md"
                         "docs/research/agent-platform/landing/inv-lifecycle-storage-opus-2026-09-26.md"
                         "docs/seon/issues/call-preparation-snapshot-answers-an-older-database-with-a-newer-program.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "a-positional-database-is-not-supplied"
             :kind :function
             :intent "Defaults are supplied by declared schema name for a request-map key but not for a positional argument: (tagged :probe) against [:=> [:cat :seon.db/database-value :keyword] ...] refuses argument count. Spec 1.13 says every function."
             :must-read #{seon.call-preparation/prepare seon.call-preparation/supply}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/dogfood-author-opus-2026-09-26.md"
                         "docs/research/agent-platform/language-requirements-2026-09-24.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "the-call-state-is-an-atom"
             :kind :function
             :intent "The call-state atom (atom audit A008/A009) still holds plans and the snapshot; the direct pure-memo replacement cost +2.4 us per call (+28%, 0.50 -> 2.94 us) on a hook that runs on every SCI Var call. Design recorded: key the projection-held memo by commit identity first, call internals unarmed, hold plans in a projection-held LRU keyed by revision key plus symbol."
             :must-read #{seon.call-preparation/hook seon.call-preparation/snapshot}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/landing/delete-r8-r6-r10-2026-09-26.md"}}]
